-- title:
--   Blow-up chart of a local Drinfeld chart at a parameter
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField O` is algebraically closed and carries an algebra structure over `GaloisField q 2`, and assume `CoordRing q κ` — the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1` — is a domain. Let $\pi$ generate $\mathfrak m_O$, let $\varpi \in \mathfrak m_O$ be non-zero, and let `pr` be a chart presentation, i.e. power series $f,u,v \in O[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$; put $S = O[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\varpi^{q+1})v - fu)$ and assume the image of $\varpi$ in $S$ is a non-zero-divisor. Write $L$ for the localisation of $S$ away from that image, $\iota_0 : O \to L$ for the structural map, $x_0 = X_0/\varpi$, $x_1 = X_1/\varpi$ in $L$, and $R \subseteq L$ for the subring generated by the image of $S$ together with $x_0,x_1$. The assertion is that $\iota_0(O) \subseteq R$, $x_0,x_1 \in R$, that $R$ is Noetherian, that $P = (\iota_0\pi) \subseteq R$ is prime, and that there are a $\kappa$-algebra structure on $R/P$ with $\operatorname{residue}(a) \mapsto \iota_0(a) \bmod P$, a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e_R : R/P \cong$ `CoordRing q κ`, and $c \in \kappa$ with: every element of $S$ of the form $C a + X_0g_0 + X_1g_1$ with $a \in \mathfrak m_O$ lies in $R$ and in $P$; $c \neq 0$ and $c^{q+1}\overline{u(0)} = \overline{v(0)}$; $e_R(x_0) = c\,$`x q κ` and $e_R(x_1) = c\,$`y q κ`; and, finally, the localisation of $R$ at $P$ is a domain and a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\iota_0\pi$, whose residue field carries a $\kappa$-algebra structure compatible with $\operatorname{residue}$ on $O$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism onto `drinfeldFunctionField q κ` $=$ `FractionRing (CoordRing q κ)` which, on the image of every $r \in R$, agrees with $e_R(r \bmod P)$ viewed in the fraction field.
--
--   This is the blow-up chart computation for the local Drinfeld chart, carried out purely ring-theoretically (no integrality of $S$ and no valuation subring of a fraction field is assumed) and at a parameter $\varpi$ that need not be a uniformiser, as happens after a tame base change; it identifies the special fibre of the chart $S[X_0/\varpi, X_1/\varpi]$ with the affine Drinfeld curve and the associated local ring with a discrete valuation ring having the Drinfeld function field as residue field. It is used in the construction of the auxiliary full-level model of the modular curve, via [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_localBlowupChart_ringHom_coordRing_of_chartPresentation_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_localBlowupChart_ringHom_coordRing_of_chartPresentation_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors), and is obtained by combining the corresponding statement about $R/P$ with the criterion [`IsLocalRing.isDomain_and_isPrincipalIdealRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_singleton`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.isDomain_and_isPrincipalIdealRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_singleton).
